160 THE BANGLADESH GAZETTE, EXTRA., JANUARY 11, 1984
84/41, dated the 26th January, 1983, the Government is pleased to declare the
constitution of a Upazila Parishad consisting of the following, namely :—

(a) Chairman (to be elected);
(b) representative members (Chairman of the Union Parishads and
Paurashavas within the Upazila, ex-officio);
(০) three women members residing in the Upazila (to be nominated by
the Government);
(d) official members as under:
(i) Upazila Nirbahi Officer. ex-officio;
(ii) Upazila Health and Family Planning Officer, ex-officio;
(iii) Upazila Education Officer, ex-officio;
(iv) Upazila Agriculture Officer, ex-officio;
(v) Upazila Engineer, ex-officio;
(vi) Upazila Co-operative Officer, ex-officio;
(vii) Upazila Livestock Officer, ex-officio;
(viii) Upazila Fishery Officer, ex-officio;
(ix) Upazila Social Welfare Officer, ex-officio;
(x) Upazila Rural Development Officer, ex-officio;
(xi) Upazila Mass Communication Officer, ex-officio;
(xii) Upazila Revenue Officer, ex-officio; and
(xiii) Officer-in-charge, Police Station, ex-officio.
. (e) Chairman of the Thana Central Co-operative Association within the
Upazila; and :
(0 One member (to be nominated by the Government).
(2) Until the Chairman is elected and enters upon his office, the Upazila
Mirbahi Officer shall act as Chairman of the Upazila Parishad.
; By order of the President
A. EK. AZAD
; Pc hs Deputy Secretary.
