Provided that the Government may, before expiry of such term, in the
public interest, discharge any member nominated, without showing any cause,
and the members so nominated may also resign their office at any time, by
writing under their hands, addressed to the Chairman.
9. Meetings of the Board, etc.—(1) The Board may, subject to the other
provisions of this section, determine the procedure of its meetings.

